cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it, together with CelluloseForge and the force fields and tools listed under references."
title: "Cellulose_interface: cellulose–liquid interface workflow for GROMACS"
type: software
version: 0.8.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
authors:
  - family-names: "Sridhar"
    given-names: "Arun Srikanth"
repository-code: "https://github.com/askforarun/Cellulose_interface"
abstract: >-
  Builds a crystalline GLYCAM cellulose slab with CelluloseForge, parameterizes
  a small-molecule liquid with GAFF2/AM1-BCC or uses a rigid water preset, packs
  the liquid on both cellulose surfaces, and writes one combined GROMACS system
  in which each force field keeps its own 1–4 scaling.
keywords:
  - cellulose
  - interface
  - GLYCAM
  - GAFF2
  - GROMACS
  - molecular dynamics
